   "description": "Meridian Tuxedo is defined by contrast. Its black and white dial emphasises the geometry of the sector-inspired layout, creating a distinctive yet carefully balanced appearance. Contrasting sandblasted and circular-brushed surfaces add physical depth, while polished applied numerals and hour markers lend a more refined character. The hands and applied elements are filled with Swiss Super-LumiNova BGW9 for clear blue illumination after dark. The monochrome dial is complemented by a sculpted 37mm stainless steel case with a short 43mm lug-to-lug length and slim profile. Equipped with the Miyota 9039 automatic movement, sapphire crystal and 150 metres of water resistance, Meridian Tuxedo combines dressier visual contrast with the capability of an everyday field watch.",
